Torchlight: RTSS fog colours a fragment and leaves its alpha alone, as the
fixed-function fog of OGRE 1.6 (which Torchlight ran on) does. Not
__SWITCH__-guarded (a GLSL library file; both targets need it). FFP_PixelFog
mixed all four channels towards the fog colour, whose alpha is 1, so a far
alpha-blended surface became opaque: the caves' POSTWATER fog plane
(media/skyboxes/cavern/fog.MESH, fog_mat, past FOG END) drew as hard-edged
fog-coloured blotches cut by its alpha_rejection over the sky dome. Only the
per-pixel path is patched: the port sets calc_mode per_pixel (renderer.cpp).

diff --git a/Media/RTShaderLib/FFPLib_Fog.glsl b/Media/RTShaderLib/FFPLib_Fog.glsl
index b57c3241c..7ce3c86f8 100644
--- a/Media/RTShaderLib/FFPLib_Fog.glsl
+++ b/Media/RTShaderLib/FFPLib_Fog.glsl
@@ -88,5 +88,7 @@ void FFP_PixelFog(in float depth,
 {
 	float fogFactor = 0.0;
 	FFP_FogFactor(depth, fogParams, fogFactor);
-	oColor = mix(fogColor, baseColor, fogFactor);
+	// Torchlight port: fixed-function fog colours a fragment and leaves its
+	// alpha alone; mixing all four channels made a far blended surface opaque.
+	oColor = vec4(mix(fogColor.rgb, baseColor.rgb, fogFactor), baseColor.a);
 }
\ No newline at end of file
